  "slug": "association-genome-8932",
  "summary": "Recent methods extend association and colocalization inference to admixed, related, and multi-ancestry cohorts with calibrated error control.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extending genetic association and colocalization inference beyond single-ancestry, unrelated cohorts while maintaining calibrated error rates. Tractor-Mix adapts local-ancestry-informed Tractor GWAS to admixed cohorts with relatedness, yielding ancestry-specific association. Four multi-ancestry colocalization methods pair SuSiEx or MsCAVIAR fine-mapping with coloc or eCAVIAR, evaluated by simulation and applied to T2D GWAS. A transcript-aware rare-variant aggregation framework applied to All of Us cardiopulmonary traits reports calibrated false-positive rates and competitive power. DPCGS addresses the downstream step, linking GWAS summary statistics to scRNA-seq data through calibrated gene-set scoring. Other items apply related computational logic to copy number variant detection from genotyping array signals and to allele-specific guide design from population variant data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-26"
}
